    <informations>Shelly EM — mounting view.
Terminals, left to right as printed: P1+ P1− P2+ P2− L O N.

Official sources:
https://kb.shelly.cloud/knowledge-base/shelly-em
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_3001015d4fc4077bd354529c1a1be75ad0d72c5a1c419b7a8bd2fd887705c0e4/image-20220920-072542.png?cb=c975bebccda45ad8749c3c18169d0714
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_400c6a9efe0c673c55d0009d82daefc0fde36c109776771897a4480febf34b31/EM-Gen1-wiring%20diagram.png?cb=85d32a50c1f168e52ca0e3f6ac6fd1a8
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_a58397532ba3bfce0343dcbfd358a2c3461225a0f6783144b3ca565e444e6ace/User%20and%20Safety%20Guide?cb=56945fa9c281e680ef71bd79ebcf8e54

Notes:
- Original EM uses screw connections for both CT pairs, unlike EM Gen3/Gen4 CT sockets.

Open points:
- Legacy KB lists Size 39mm x 36mm x 17mm without axis labels. W=39/H=36 is the conventional product-view interpretation, not an explicit axis-labelled source.

Nominal dimensions and an illustrative outline: corner radii, screw pitch and recesses are drawn to be recognisable, not to manufacturing CAD.</informations>
